    sets := #["msh"] },
  { id := 118, comment := "Effects other than Mjölnir's equip worthy ability that cause it to become attached to a creature can attach it to a creature that isn't worthy. For example, suppose you control a Mjölnir that isn't attached to anything as well as Loki, God of Mischief (a blue God Sorcerer Villain creature) with Super-Soldier Serum (an Aura with \"Whenever enchanted creature attacks or blocks, attach any number of target Equipment you control to it.\") attached to him. When Loki attacks, you can target Mjölnir with Super-Soldier Serum's ability, and when that ability resolves, Mjölnir will become attached to Loki. (It doesn't have to be Loki, but it's more fun that way.)",
    cards := #["Mjölnir, Hammer of Thor"],
    sets := #["msh"] },
  { id := 119, comment := "Equip worthy is a variant of the equip keyword. \"Equip worthy [cost]\" means \"[Cost]: Attach this Equipment to target legendary non-Villain creature you control that's red and/or white. Activate only as a sorcery.\"",
